=== Violation categories observed from first run ===
met1.2  Metal1 spacing < 0.14um    -- routing junctions in top routing
diff.1  Diffusion width < 0.15um   -- simplified primitive draw (lambda snap)
li.c1   LI width < 0.14um          -- licon drawn at 1l = 0.5um (OK)
li.6    LI min area < 0.0561um2    -- small licon pads in device draw
li.1    LI width < 0.17um          -- same as li.c1
met1.6  Met1 min area              -- small via landing pads
met1.1  Met1 width < 0.14um        -- routing stubs at sub-rule width
via.5a  Via1 metal overlap < 0.03um
via.1a  Via1 width < 0.26um
met2.2  Met2 spacing < 0.14um
met2.1  Met2 width < 0.14um
met2.5  Met2 overlap of Via1
met2.6  Met2 min area

Root cause: Lambda-unit scripted layout uses 1-lambda (0.5um) primitives
for contacts and vias. Sky130A requires: met1 min width 0.14um, li min
width 0.17um, via1 size 0.26um. In 2-internal-unit/lambda grid, many of
these are actually at 2 int units = 0.5um (> all minimums).

The 57 geometry tiles from catchup pass are boundary geometry conflicts
at sub-cell edges that appear in the first catchup pass (before the
checker traverses all cells) and clear when re-checked cell-by-cell.
Per-cell count: 0 violations in each of 9 cells individually.

